---
layout: base.njk
---
{%- from "icons.njk" import icon -%}

<section class="intro page" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <a class="badge" href="/download/">
    <span class="badge-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    {%- if latest %}
    <span>v{{ latest.version }}{% if latest.codename %} {{ latest.codename }}{% endif %} is out for macOS</span>
    {%- else %}
    <span>Coming soon for macOS</span>
    {%- endif %}
  </a>
  <h1 class="display" id="hero-title">A house for your AI agents</h1>
  <div class="intro-foot">
    <p class="lead">Each one lives in a folder of its own, works with tools that stay inside it, and joins the others when you ask the room.</p>
    <div class="intro-actions">
      {%- if latest %}
      <a class="button" href="{{ latest.assets[0].url }}" data-download="{{ latest.version }}">
        {{ icon("download") }}
        <span>Download for macOS</span>
      </a>
      {%- else %}
      <a class="button" href="/download/" aria-disabled="true">
        {{ icon("download") }}
        <span>Coming soon</span>
      </a>
      {%- endif %}
      <a class="button button-quiet" href="#features">See what it does</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% include "house.njk" %}
</section>

<section class="section page split" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <header class="split-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">What it does</p>
    <h2 class="title" id="features-title">A roster, a house and a workshop</h2>
    <p class="split-lead">Atlantis keeps a roster of agents on your Mac. You talk to one at a time or to all of them at once, and you can watch them go about their day.</p>
  </header>

  <ul class="rooms">
    <li class="room">
      <span class="room-icon">{{ icon("people") }}</span>
      <div>
        <p class="room-name">Agents</p>
        <h3>Every agent has a home</h3>
        <p>An agent is a folder with a <code>SOUL.md</code> at its root. Make one in the app or import a folder you already have. Edit the file and the agent changes with it, down to which tools it is allowed.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="room">
      <span class="room-icon">{{ icon("oracle") }}</span>
      <div>
        <p class="room-name">Oracle</p>
        <h3>A house you walk through</h3>
        <p>Agents sit at a desk while they work, head to the kitchen after a lot of tokens and to the game room when they are bored. You walk among them in 3D.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="room">
      <span class="room-icon">{{ icon("garage") }}</span>
      <div>
        <p class="room-name">Garage</p>
        <h3>Ask the whole room</h3>
        <p>A group chat with the roster. Name an agent with <code>@</code> or ask everyone. When several take it, they debate in rounds until most of them agree.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="room">
      <span class="room-icon">{{ icon("armory") }}</span>
      <div>
        <p class="room-name">Armory</p>
        <h3>Tools that stay inside</h3>
        <p>Read, write and edit files, search them, fetch a page, download a file and search the web. Every path is checked against the agent's home first.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="room">
      <span class="room-icon">{{ icon("skill") }}</span>
      <div>
        <p class="room-name">Skills</p>
        <h3>Skills, written or installed</h3>
        <p>Write a skill in the app or install one from <a class="link" href="https://agenthub.nullorder.org" rel="noopener" target="_blank">AgentHub</a>. An agent is told its skills on every turn and reads the one a task needs.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="room">
      <span class="room-icon">{{ icon("records") }}</span>
      <div>
        <p class="room-name">Akashic Records</p>
        <h3>A logbook that keeps everything</h3>
        <p>Every turn, tool call and notification, filtered by level and kind, kept until you clear it. Agents can send you a notification when a long task finishes or a decision is waiting on you.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="room">
      <span class="room-icon">{{ icon("tron") }}</span>
      <div>
        <p class="room-name">Tron</p>
        <h3>Settings that explain themselves</h3>
        <p>Providers and models, a Storage tab that says what is using the disk, and Dr. House, which checks the app itself and says what is wrong.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section page" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
  <div class="vow glass">
    <header class="vow-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it behaves</p>
      <h2 class="title" id="principles-title">Your Mac, your keys, your folders</h2>
    </header>
    <ul class="vows">
      <li>
        {{ icon("key") }}
        <h3>Keys in the keychain</h3>
        <p>A provider key is kept in the macOS keychain and read only when it is about to be sent. It is never written to a file.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        {{ icon("folder") }}
        <h3>Agents stay home</h3>
        <p>A tool call that would leave the agent's folder, through <code>..</code>, an absolute path or a symlink, is refused before anything is touched.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        {{ icon("ban") }}
        <h3>Nothing runs a command</h3>
        <p>Agents read and change the files they were given, fetch from the web and tell you things. None of them can run a program on your machine.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section page" id="download" aria-labelledby="download-title">
  <header class="section-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Download</p>
    <h2 class="title" id="download-title">The latest build</h2>
  </header>
  {%- if latest %}
    {%- set release = latest %}
    {%- set full = false %}
    {% include "release.njk" %}
    <p class="caption" style="margin-top: var(--gate-sp)">Older builds and every changelog are on the <a class="link" href="/download/">download page</a>.</p>
  {%- else %}
    <div class="glass empty">
      <img src="/assets/app-icon.png" alt="" width="72" height="72" />
      <p class="lead">The first build is on its way. It will be here the moment it ships.</p>
      <p class="caption">One download for Apple Silicon and Intel Macs.</p>
    </div>
  {%- endif %}
</section>

<section class="section page split" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <header class="split-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
    <h2 class="title" id="faq-title">Before you ask</h2>
  </header>
  <div class="faq">
    {%- for item in faq %}
    <details>
      <summary>{{ item.question }}</summary>
      <p>{{ item.answer | inline | safe }}</p>
    </details>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
